            "modified": "2026-08-18T12:55:22.180691Z",
            "name": "Debugger Evasion",
            "description": "[confidence=high, sources=static] The malware string 'IsDebuggerPresent' was found in the binary. This string is characteristic of Debugger Evasion behavior. The presence of this specific string alone (no other Debugger Evasion-related string corroborates it) indicates the malware has capabilities associated with this technique, but with less certainty than a corroborated combination would. | The API functions IsDebuggerPresent, SetUnhandledExceptionFilter are all imported by the binary. This combination is characteristic of Debugger Evasion \u2014 multiple corroborating APIs together, not one import in isolation, is what makes this a strong signal. | YARA rule 'AntiDebug_IsDebuggerPresent' matched the sample. This rule was specifically designed to detect Debugger Evasion patterns, confirming the presence of this capability.",
            "external_references": [
                {
                    "source_name": "mitre-attack",
                    "url": "https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1622/",
                    "external_id": "T1622"
                }
            ],
            "x_confidence": "high",
